# Phase 59: Nucleus Daemon (Unified Runtime)
**Goal:** Implement the "Presence-Aware" Daemon as a parallel service.
**Strategy:** Non-Destructive Additive Build.

## 1. Core Infrastructure (Additive)
*   [ ] **Module:** Create `mcp_server_nucleus/daemon/` package (The Unified Runtime).
*   [ ] **Service Class:** Implement `NucleusDaemon` with `asyncio` loop in `mcp_server_nucleus/daemon/runtime.py`.
*   [ ] **Entry Point:** Use `python -m mcp_server_nucleus.daemon` (Native Module Execution).
    *   *Note:* This explicitly moves away from `scripts/` to a first-class module structure.

## 2. Presence Monitor (The Sensor)
*   [ ] **Logic:** Implement `PresenceMonitor` in `mcp_server_nucleus/daemon/presence.py`.
    *   **Check 1:** `EventsTail` check (Reading `events.jsonl` for `user_intent` or [interaction](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py#103-134)).
    *   **Check 2:** `ProcessMap` check (Using [ps](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/capabilities/code_ops.py#7-128) to find [code](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#4587-4663) or `cursor` processes).
*   [ ] **State:** Maintain `UserStatus` (ONLINE/OFFLINE) in memory.

## 3. Internal Orchestrator (The Runtime)
*   [ ] **Integration:** Import [SwarmsOrchestrator](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/orchestrator.py#8-157) directly into `NucleusDaemon`.
*   [ ] **Trigger:** When `UserStatus == OFFLINE` (> 5 mins):
    *   Verify [state.json](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/autonomous_state.json) lock.
    *   If free, Trigger `SwarmsOrchestrator.run_maintenance_loop()`.
    *   *Goal:* Pure internal execution. No subprocess shell calls.

## 4. Verification (The Proof)
*   [ ] **Simulated Test:** `python scripts/verify_daemon.py`.
    *   Mock "User Active" -> Daemon Sleeps.
    *   Mock "User Offline" -> Daemon Wakes.

## 5. Safety
*   [ ] **Isolation:** The Daemon will use a separate log file `daemon.log`.
*   [ ] **No Conflict:** It will respect the [state.json](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/autonomous_state.json) locking mechanism (Atomic Claims) so it plays nice with any manual scripts running.
